NON-EQUIVALENT, proven input. ingest/src/main/java/binjava/ingest/Window.java:
    package binjava.ingest;
    record Window(long lo, long hi) {
      long now() { return hi; }
      long span(Window window) { return window.now() - lo; }
    }
At the staged bytes: clean, exit 0. Under the mutation: `Window.java:4: .now() reaches the real clock directly`, exit 1 -- a file that touches no clock refused as sourcing the real one.

WHY IT IS MAJOR AND NOT A STYLE POINT. (a) The production docstring makes this exact claim and sources it to a measurement: '⚠️ THE RECEIVER MUST LOOK LIKE A TYPE. ... `window.now()` is a record accessor reaching nothing -- review MEASURED the unanchored form refusing a file that touched no clock.' The regression it guards against ALREADY HAPPENED once in this task's history and nothing in the suite would notice it happening again. (b) The suite pins the SIBLING false-refusal anchor and not this one: anIdentifierENDINGInABannedNameIsNotAViolation exists solely because `dataFiles.size()` was reported as `Files.` reaching the filesystem, and its javadoc states the principle -- 'A FALSE REFUSAL IS HOW A GATE GETS WEAKENED ... the direction non-negotiable 2 forbids' -- so the omission is asymmetric rather than a judgement that the direction does not matter. (c) The real-tree case cannot cover it: I checked, no non-exempt src/main file has a lowercase-receiver `.now()` today (`git grep -nE '[a-z_$][\\w$]*\\s*(\\.|::)\\s*now\\s*\\(' -- '*/src/main/java/binjava/*.java'` is empty), so the tree is green by luck.

